---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About">

  <section style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;">

    <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">About</h1>

    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #333; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Energy Ledger is an independent, open source resource exploring how energy systems verify the claims they make — and how emerging cryptographic technology could make that verification more granular, more private, and more trustworthy.
    </p>

    <p style="color: #333; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      The project sits at the intersection of energy policy and blockchain technology. It is not affiliated with any company, institution, or blockchain project.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Why this exists</h2>

    <p style="color: #333; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Energy markets run on certificates, declarations, and reports. Guarantees of Origin, renewable energy certificates, demand response confirmations, prosumer feed-in records — these documents underpin billions of euros in markets and regulatory compliance obligations.
    </p>

    <p style="color: #333; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Most of these systems were designed before modern cryptography made it possible to prove things about data without revealing the data itself. Energy Ledger explores what becomes possible when that gap closes.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Open source</h2>

    <p style="color: #333; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      This site and all its content are open source. Corrections, contributions, and new explainers are welcome.
    </p>

    <a href="https://github.com/energyledgernet" style="display: inline-block; background: #0c3530; color: #3abf99; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border-radius: 8px;">View on GitHub →</a>

    <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Contact</h2>

    <p style="color: #333;">
      Questions or suggestions — <a href="mailto:hello@energyledger.net">hello@energyledger.net</a>
    </p>

  </section>

</BaseLayout>